    <GaugingStation location="Rosehall" name="Cassley" number="3004">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station with some of the regime influenced by a hydroelectric power scheme.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Cableway at a 35m wide river section located 400m downstream of the stage measuring site. Adequately gauged to bankfull.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity area station. Stable gabion groyne control adequately gauged to bankfull. Station added to peak flows dataset in August 2025 (WINFAP Files v14).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Nov-Dec 2010 flows considered suspect due to extended period of freezing conditions.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Runoff (apart from compensation flows and spillage) from 14% of the upper catchment is diverted to the Shin hydroelectric power scheme. No significant surface storage.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Typical Highland mix of rough grazing and moorland with some afforestation.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">H</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged to 2.960m with a measured flow of 219 cumecs. Floods spill out of bank around the station hut at around 2.7m." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="With a limited floodplain component, the extrapolation of the in-channel calibration will likely give a reasonable estimation of events above 3m, and hence this station is tentatively assigned pooling status." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
